VeridianOS: plasma-apply-aurorae runs with /bin/sh

The script (plasma-apply-aurorae.cmake) names /usr/bin/bash as its
interpreter, which systems without bash -- or with it elsewhere -- do not
have, so applying an Aurorae decoration failed there. It uses nothing
beyond POSIX sh (tests, quoted "$@", exit), so it now runs with /bin/sh.

--- a/plasma-apply-aurorae.cmake
+++ b/plasma-apply-aurorae.cmake
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#!/usr/bin/bash
+#!/bin/sh
 
 # TODO Plasma 7: Drop aurorae.knsrc, use knsrc file provided by KWin.
 
